---

## Recommendations

### 1. Dedicated Bug Resolution Team
- Establish a team specifically tasked with addressing smaller client concerns.
- Assign customer advocates to maintain communication and ensure transparency.

### 2. Improved Communication Channels
- Implement a client-facing bug tracker to provide real-time updates on issue resolution.
- Train customer support staff to deliver detailed and personalized responses.

### 3. Balanced Development Strategy
- Reassess development priorities to include customer-requested updates alongside AI-driven features.
- Schedule quarterly reviews to ensure smaller client needs are being addressed.

### 4. Proactive Engagement
- Host regular feedback sessions with smaller clients to understand their needs.
- Offer incentives for smaller clients to remain engaged and provide constructive feedback.

---

## Conclusion
The feedback from smaller clients highlights the urgent need for improved communication, prioritization of their concerns, and a balanced approach to development. Addressing these issues promptly will help restore trust and prevent further strain on client relationships.

